# PowerShell-safe Git commits

When creating git commits in this repo on Windows/PowerShell:

- **Single invocation:** Run `git add` and `git commit` in one terminal command (e.g. `git add ... ; git commit -m $title -m $body`). Use `required_permissions: ['all']` when the agent runs git.
- **No bash syntax:** Do not use bash heredocs or bash-style redirections (they fail in PowerShell). Use `git commit -m "<title>" -m "<body>"` or PowerShell here-strings.
- **Scoped commits:** If the user asks to commit "web" (or similar), stage only `web/**` and `README.md` if relevant. Do not stage `.cursor/**` or untracked `scripts/` unless explicitly requested.

## Example

```powershell
$title = '[TAG] component: short description'
$body = @'
WHY: Explain why this change was made.

Optional details if needed.
'@
git add -- "README.md" "web"; if ($?) { git commit -m $title -m $body }
```
